"orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cancan","key":"wangpedh","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Laura","key":"junckerjensenpedh","last":"Juncker-Jensen","name":"Juncker-Jensen, Laura","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788794538039"],"pages":"1-4","place":"Copenhagen","status":"p","title":"Action Research Booklet"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-39fbc1c5-859b-4512-ace2-abfff8eb891d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A case of action research with a focus on collective learning about organisational challenges and solutions for democratically owned businesses","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789548","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This discussion paper commenced by inquiring what needs to be done to unleash the full potential of data for the sustainability transformation. Each section subsequently provided propositions that serve as a roadmap for exploring how data management approaches can be optimized to support sustainable development goals. Overall, this discussion provides a frame of reference for research, for example for sustainability reporting approaches (i.e., regulatory non-financial reporting and carbon-reporting approaches), impact measurement and valuation method, and data activities (i.e., data management, data processes and data sourcing). This will allow Information Systems scholars some guidance in approaching the role of data in the sustainability transformation. We argue that it is important to consider the choice of different sustainability reporting approaches and their alignment with the choice of impact measurement and valuation method as well as data strategies and practices, when tackling corporate sustainability transformation,. We call for future IS research to explore the connection between these dimensions and how the interplay of the reporting approaches, impact measurement and valuation method, and data activities shape corporate sustainability transformation, in the truest sense of the word.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Püchel, Lea","Wang, Cancan","Buhmann, Karin","Brandt, Tobias","von Schweinitz, Felizia","Marie Edinger-Schons, Laura","vom Brocke, Jan","Legner, Christine","Teracino, Elizabeth","Daniel Mardahl, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-086.40-768095"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Püchel, Lea"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Research Center for Information Systems (ERCIS)","HEC Lausanne","University of Hamburg","University of Lausanne","University of Munster","University of Münster","Université de Lausanne"],"keyword":["Sustainability transformation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Independent Researcher"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the pivotal role of data in sustainability transformations challenges and opportunities","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12599-024-00904-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.40-768095","identifier":[{"id":"85207240079","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-cb357baa-d16d-4684-b4b5-e0143e5e294f","itu-a0678acb-f2a8-427b-8312-3b0f6641893d"],"keyword":["Sustainability Data","Sustainability Transformation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-706EA6B9FDFAC85DD664F09FB958771F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107275866/s12599-024-00904-4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/109332935/s12599-024-00904-4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12599-024-00904-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of munster","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Munster","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"european research center for information systems","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"European Research Center for Information Systems (ERCIS)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of münster","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Münster","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"