Christensen, Hilda","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bettina","key":"haugeped","last":"Hauge","name":"Hauge, Bettina","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Cancan","key":"wangped","last":"Wang","locid":"3e29e63c-70b6-4043-9f89-78f6de293337","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9787542661364"],"pages":"185","place":"Shanghai","publisher":"Shanghai Joint Publishing Company","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-194cd835-1b07-4043-bba9-44b7be624913"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"女性、性别与研究 : 中国与北欧视角","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-277766","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The notion of adaptive governance was originally created to capture forms of collaboration in socio-ecological systems that can respond to rapid changes in the environment. However, such a notion also has a great potential to be transferred and understood in the digital government context, where there is an increasing need to establish forms of collaboration that can respond to swift changes in the environment related to technology and citizen demands. Drawing on the analysis of four cases of IT-related project collaboration, we put forward that the degree of sharing of decision-making power and of accountability between government and non-government actors is critical to developing different types of adaptive governance. Findings show that the distribution of decision-making power and of accountability can be decoupled, resulting in three types of adaptive governance – namely polycentric, agile, and organic governance. We contribute to research by detailing and empirically testing the notion of adaptive governance in a digital government context, and to practice by highlighting the role of the distribution of decision-making power and of accountability in devising adaptive governance strategies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wang, Cancan","Medaglia, Rony","Zheng, Lei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-291207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fudan University"],"keyword":["Accountability","Adaptive governance","Decision making","Digital government"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a typology of adaptive governance in the digital government context the role of decision making and accountability","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-291207","identifier":[{"id":"85028720331","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-a6226721-2185-4492-9872-d4f93107cc16"],"keyword":["Accountability","Adaptive governance","Decision-making","Digital government"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8DA7819B8D4C9D48977B08FFDA0522FC"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"fudan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fudan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cancan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"3e29e63c-70b6-4043-9f89-78f6de293337","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rony","key":"medagliapau","last":"Medaglia","locid":"12758b5f-b20b-4031-8b26-35dc5a91095c","name":"Medaglia, Rony","orcid":"0000-0001-7292-5895","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Lei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.giq.2017.08.003","issn":["0740624X","18729517"],"issn_org":["0740624X"],"journal":"Government Information Quarterly","pages":"306-322","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Government Information Quarterly","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028720331"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-a6226721-2185-4492-9872-d4f93107cc16"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Towards a Typology of Adaptive Governance in the Digital Government Context : The Role of Decision-making and Accountability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-291207","year":"2018","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Abrahamson, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-403947"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["China","Denmark","Det Samfundsvidenskabelige Fakultet","Elderly care","Welfare systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"丹麦和中国视角 下的性别和福利制度调整","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-403947","ids":["ku-11ba7674-94da-4efb-8827-379b5156d44d"],"keyword":["China","Denmark","Det Samfundsvidenskabelige Fakultet","elderly care","welfare systems"],"lang":"Chinese","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-967302C3FD9BD9A4F769BB2F68A09A2D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Asian Dynamics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Department of Sociology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"abrahamsonpau","last":"Abrahamson","locid":"01346743-644d-4741-b02a-7cd3fc74d8d8","name":"Abrahamson, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hilda","key":"rømerchristensenpedh","last":"Rømer Christensen","name":"Rømer Christensen, Hilda","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bettina","key":"haugepedh","last":"Hauge","name":"Hauge, Bettina","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cancan","key":"wangpedh","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9787542661364"],"pages":"91-109","place":"Shanghai","publisher":"Shanghai Joint Publishing House","status":"p","subtitle":"中国与北欧视角","title":"女性，性别与研究"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-11ba7674-94da-4efb-8827-379b5156d44d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"丹麦和中国视角 : 下的性别和福利制度调整","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-403947","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: As social media technologies permeate public life, the current forms of collaboration between government and non-government stakeholders are changing. The purpose of this paper is to investigate how social media use reconfigures the organizing practices around such collaboration. A case study of a collaborative e-government project showcases how emergent organizing practices through external social media differ from existing ones along the dimensions of time, task, team, and transition. Design/methodology/approach: This paper presents a case study of a collaborative e-government project on open data, organized by Shanghai Municipality, local businesses, universities, and NGOs, using an external social media platform, WeChat. Adopting the theoretical lens of temporary organization, the paper identifies the key aspects of change emerged in the organizing practices of this collaboration. Findings: The findings outline how the use of external social media reconfigures the collaboration between government and non-government stakeholders along the four dimensions of time, task, team, and transition. The new form of collaboration is reconfigured along the lines of: an ad-hoc and non-linear management of time; Discursive task creation, assignment and engagement among stakeholders; a serendipitous engagement of team members based on expertise; and (4) shifiting formal and informal organizing practices. Originality/value: This paper provides insights on the use of external social media for collaboration in e-government research, and develops the concept of temporary organization in a sociomaterial setting. It also provides practical suggestions on how to manage new forms of public projects leveraging on the capacity of external social media.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Wang, Cancan","Medaglia, Rony"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-286690"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["E government","Inter organizational collaboration","Social media","Temporary organization"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"governments social media use for external collaboration juggling time task team and transition with technology","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/57187720/rony_medaglia_governments_social_media_use_acceptedmanuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-286690","identifier":[{"id":"85038261699","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000417487700004","type":"wos"}],"ids":["cbs-764f3f5f-a7ca-4109-99f6-2668d1fca8e8"],"keyword":["E-government","Inter-organizational collaboration","Social media","Temporary organization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0007BA918C258995526DDBA90BEB305E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/57187720/rony_medaglia_governments_social_media_use_acceptedmanuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cancan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"3e29e63c-70b6-4043-9f89-78f6de293337","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rony","key":"medagliapau","last":"Medaglia","locid":"12758b5f-b20b-4031-8b26-35dc5a91095c","name":"Medaglia, Rony","orcid":"0000-0001-7292-5895","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/tg-02-2017-0009","issn":["17506166","17506174"],"issn_org":["17506166"],"issue":"4","journal":"Transforming Government","pages":"572-595","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing","status":"p","title":"Transforming Government","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85038261699"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-764f3f5f-a7ca-4109-99f6-2668d1fca8e8"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Governments’ Social Media Use for External Collaboration : Juggling Time, Task, Team, and Transition, with Technology","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-286690","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"As the body of Information Systems (IS) research on social media grows, it faces increasing challenges of staying relevant to real world contexts. In this research-in-progress paper, we analyze and contrast research on social media in the e-government field and in IS research, by reviewing and categorizing 63 studies published in key journal outlets, in order to identify and complement research foci and gaps. We find that in comparison with e-government social media research, IS studies tend to adopt an abstract view of the individual user, focus on a monetary view of value added by social media, and overlook the role of contextual factors. We thus propose an extended framework for mapping social media research, by including a focus on the role of context and environment, and identify a research agenda for future studies on social media-related phenomena relevant to real world contexts.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wang, Cancan","Medaglia, Rony","Sæbø, Øystein"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-299386"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-01","place":"Chiayi, tw","start":"2016-06-27","title":"The 20th Pacific Asia Conference on Information Systems. PACIS 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Agder"],"keyword":["E business","E government","Literature review","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learning from e government an agenda for social media research in is","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.pacis2016.org/Abstract/ALL/711.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-299386","ids":["cbs-fb44e3c1-54ca-4467-89ce-3c9b304205c9"],"keyword":["E-business","E-government","Literature review","Social media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-85B89225D24308B478B915CEE2BEC46D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.pacis2016.org/Abstract/ALL/711.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of agder","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Agder","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cancan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"3e29e63c-70b6-4043-9f89-78f6de293337","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rony","key":"medagliapau","last":"Medaglia","locid":"12758b5f-b20b-4031-8b26-35dc5a91095c","name":"Medaglia, Rony","orcid":"0000-0001-7292-5895","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Øystein","key":"sæbøpau","last":"Sæbø","name":"Sæbø, Øystein","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Patrick Y.K.","key":"chaupedh","last":"Chau","name":"Chau, Patrick Y.K.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"She-I","key":"changpedh","last":"Chang","name":"Chang, She-I","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789860491029"],"place":"Atlanta, GA","publisher":"Association for Information Systems. AIS Electronic Library (AISeL)","status":"p","title":"PACIS 2016 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-fb44e3c1-54ca-4467-89ce-3c9b304205c9"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Learning from E-government : An Agenda for Social Media Research in IS","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-299386","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The nature of inter-organizational collaboration between government and other stakeholders is rapidly changing with the introduction of open social media (OSM) platforms. Characterized by a high degree of informality as well as a blurred personal/professional nature, OSM can potentially introduce changes and tensions in the well-established routines of the public sector. This paper aims at shedding light on such changes, presenting findings from a study on the use of an OSM platform, WeChat, in an interorganizational collaboration project between government, university, and industry stakeholders in China. Drawing on the framework of the theory of temporary organizations, we analyze data from interviews and participant observations to single out the characteristics of inter-organizational collaboration afforded by OSM. The findings outline the features of collaboration practices afforded by OSM in the four dimensions of time, task, team, and transition. Specifically, we report on new collaboration procedures that are characterized by an ad-hoc and non-linear management of time; a sense of shared commitment to the accomplishment of tasks; a serendipitous recruitment of team members based on expertise rather than on organizational affiliation; and a transition from formal to informal as well as from professional to private collaboration.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wang, Cancan","Medaglia, Rony","Jensen, Tina Blegind"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-283068"],"event":{"acronym":"DG.O","end":"2016-06-10","place":"Shanghai, cn","start":"2016-06-08","title":"17th Annual International Conference on Digital Government Research. dg.o 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affordances","Inter organizational collaboration","Public sector","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mobilizing government inter organizational collaboration using open social media platforms","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-283068","identifier":[{"id":"84978744390","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-50ba26b2-a9a8-4821-affc-ac38a580853b"],"keyword":["Affordances","Inter-organizational Collaboration","Public Sector","Social Media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86434E429F89DA99E966298EB21F453A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cancan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"3e29e63c-70b6-4043-9f89-78f6de293337","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rony","key":"medagliapau","last":"Medaglia","locid":"12758b5f-b20b-4031-8b26-35dc5a91095c","name":"Medaglia, Rony","orcid":"0000-0001-7292-5895","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Blegind","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5733d9c1-e4a9-426d-84bb-a5d5dd1a8973","name":"Jensen, Tina Blegind","orcid":"0000-0003-3095-1344","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yushim","key":"kimpedh","last":"Kim","name":"Kim, Yushim","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Shuhua Monica","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Shuhua Monica","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2912160.2912177","eisbn":["9781450343398"],"isbn":["9781450343398"],"pages":"357-365","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Internet Plus Government: New Opportunities to Solve Public Problems","title":"Proceedings of the 17th Annual International Conference on Digital Government Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978744390"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-50ba26b2-a9a8-4821-affc-ac38a580853b"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Mobilizing Government : Inter-Organizational Collaboration Using Open Social Media Platforms","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-283068","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
